# Wire format

`Command`, `RadioEvent`, `Mode`, `ServerMsg`, and the structs they carry are postcard-encoded. Postcard stores enum discriminants by **declaration index** and structs by **field order**. It is not self-describing.

- Append enum variants. Inserting or reordering one renumbers every later discriminant and breaks remote clients and `session.json` / `radio.json`.
- Display order is a separate `ALL` const (`Mode::ALL`, `Backend` picker). Declaration order is the wire.
- Adding or reordering a field on a struct that already rides the wire (`DigiConfig`, `DigiStatus`, `RadioState`, `QsoRecord`, …) changes every message that contains it. Bump `PROTO_VERSION` in `crates/sdroxide-proto/src/lib.rs` and add a one-line note beside the existing version history.
- `Backend` and `Mode` also appear in JSON config. Renaming a variant needs a serde alias so old files still load.
- A new `Mode` is appended, then listed in `Mode::ALL` where the picker should show it. Update the `--mode` clap help in `src/main.rs` when the CLI must accept the name.

Native and browser clients must agree on this layout. The wasm client links `sdroxide-types` and `sdroxide-proto` only.
